{
  "Version": 2,
  "Name": "Thelen1966-fig9-NBP-2to1",
  "Source": "A. Thelen, \"Equivalent Layers in Multilayer Filters,\" J. Opt. Soc. Am. 56, 1533-1538 (1966). doi:10.1364/JOSA.56.001533 - Fig. 9 caption, p. 1538: 1.7 | (HLH) [(6H/5)(3L/5)(6H/5)(3L/5)(6H/5)(3L/5)(6H/5)(3L/5)(6H/5)]^3 (HL'H) | 1.0, nH = 4.0, nL = 1.8, nL' = 2.2",
  "Notes": "Narrow-band-pass filter whose equivalent layer II uses a 2:1 H:L thickness ratio (6H/5, 3L/5), said to be less angle-sensitive than an equal-thickness design\nSpecification: Narrow pass band centred at lambda0/lambda = 1.\nReported: Fig. 9 (p. 1538), log %T (0.01-100 %) vs lambda0/lambda 0.95-1.05 (read from plot, approximate): top ~100 % with small ripple from about 0.983 to 1.02; T falls to 0.01 % near 0.952 and 1.05.\nNotes: Printed substrate-first; reversed so (HL'H) is next to air and (HLH) next to the 1.7 substrate. Each period has five 6H/5 (1.2 QW) and four 3L/5 (0.6 QW) layers. 33 printed layers -> 29 after merging: the junctions HL'H|6H/5 and 6H/5|HLH give 2.2-QW H, the junctions between periods give 2.4-QW H. reference_nm = 1000 arbitrary; normal incidence assumed.\nLayers from Fig. 9 caption, p. 1538: 1.7 | (HLH) [(6H/5)(3L/5)(6H/5)(3L/5)(6H/5)(3L/5)(6H/5)(3L/5)(6H/5)]^3 (HL'H) | 1.0, nH = 4.0, nL = 1.8, nL' = 2.2; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), compare with the paper: ours T > 90 % from 0.983 to 1.016; paper top ~100 % from 0.983 to 1.02; 0.01 % near 0.952 and 1.05 (read from the figure).",
  "Wavelength": [
    1000
  ],
